  "security_implications": "This chunk instantiates seed anchoring for 10 key derivation constants, synchronizes lifecycle control, and integrates the register block. Security implications: Seed constants must not be optimized away (prim_sec_anchor_buf); kmac_en_masking_i is assertion-only and becomes a covert attack surface if assertions are disabled; hard and soft output seeds must differ to prevent cross-domain key leakage; lifecycle enable must be MUBI-encoded to avoid illegal state transitions; parameter width mismatches could corrupt seed mapping; the UseOtpSeedsInsteadOfFlash mux is not visible here and could cause incorrect seed source selection.",
